      "id": 1,
      "text": "Keller was founded in 1898 by Baby Ray Peone, a local fisherman.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keller%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town moved several times starting in 1940 because of backwatering from the Grand Coulee Dam, now 18 miles north of the Columbia River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keller%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Keller History Museum began in 2012 as a vision of long‑time residents, now a hub showcasing Cross Timbers heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
